{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c","id":106733,"title":"Development Tease: Cursed Necropolis: D.C.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-05T22:20:36-07:00","id":106733,"title":"Development Tease: Cursed Necropolis: D.C.","content":"Hi, gang,<br /> <br /> Welcome to the <b>Mummy</b> forum's first-ever Development Tease -- a post offering a sneak-peek at some material from the next book up on the schedule for the line. In this case, that'd be <i>Cursed Necropolis: D.C.</i>, which is in layout now. As a resident of the District myself, I'm pleased to offer you all a look at one of the most influential merets of Arisen in all the world:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Khent-henu</b></u><br /> <br /> The power structure of the D.C. nome is headed by a single meret\u2014the Khent-henu (\u201cFirst Chorus\u201d). Their name is a declaration to the world\u2014they sing with one voice, one power, one Descent. They are indeed unified, as befits a group guided by a prophetic Mason and holding fast to the belief that it was the first true meret of mummies. Guildmasters all, the Arisen of First Chorus have forged a vision of a bold, new Irem, a city shining bright on the river. They are exemplars of the five guilds, of how the Shan\u2019iatu\u2019s paradigm stands eternally strong.<br /> <br /> Despite their long-standing alliance, the Khent-henu are far from undivided in all things, and their influence over the nome is equally far from certain. While the city is doubtless united by the elite and their shared interest in maintaining the flow of Sekhem, D.C.\u2019s power structure can be best summed up as a cold shadow war between two rival factions...<br /> <br /> Senebti!<br /> CAS","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","dat