yone with vision, and Obama definitely has that, even if it's constantly blocked by others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T07:21:10-07:00","id":109268,"title":"","content":"I just wantto see how they pull of an actual city setting with mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T10:50:45-07:00","id":109441,"title":"","content":"DC is such an Insane Guild Goldmine!<br /> Library of Congress must be Scribe Treasure! <br /> So many statues such Lincoln, and even the moved Awakening Statue hold a lot secrets probably privy to Tef-Aabhi, not to mention the Mystical Geomancy practices and other Monuments. Hell all the mummies incorporate that in the temples even if they aren't one of the Builders.<br /> Lots of important Gravesites for the Shepherds of the Shell.<br /> Money Minting and general usefulness being a vast Dedwin confluence.<br /> And as the Capitol all the Politics, laws, and even security and intelligence Agencies make it center stage of the Maa-Kep.<br /> <br /> And all of them converge on the Smithsonian which holds Relics of all types.<br /> <br /> Its a really groovy choice for a Mummy Setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T18:31:49-07:00","id":109749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=109441#post109441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DC is such an Insane Guild Goldmine!<br /> Library of Congress must be Scribe Treasure!<br /> So many statues such Lincoln, and even the moved Awakening Statue hold a lot secrets probably privy to Tef-Aabhi, not to mention the Mystical Geomancy practices and other Monuments. Hell all the mummies incorporate that in the temples even if they aren't one of the Builders.<br /> Lots of important Gravesites for the Shepherds of the Shell.<br /> Money Minting and general usefulness being a vast Dedwin confluence.<br /> And as the Capitol all the Politics, laws, and even security and intelligence Agencies make it center stage of the Maa-Kep.<br /> <br /> And all of them converge on the Smithsonian which holds Relics of all types.<br /> <br /> Its a really groovy choice for a Mummy Setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is the home city of CAS, so he knows it well I believe.<br /> <br /> Its is also a city of the dead, a modern necropolis. I believe no other city in the continent holds more monuments to dead people and an entire museum dedicated to the evils of systematic mass murder.<br /> <br /> DC is a City of the Dead no doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T22:11:14-07:00","id":109840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scutarii</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=107396#post107396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You only remember the major events of your previous Descent (at Memory 3 anyway)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think that you have the Memory status wrong. I read it that you remember past Descents at either Memory 7 or 8.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, this is an interesting start to knowing the DC area. Will there be notice of other supernaturals in our nation's capital that the nome deals with as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T22:25:26-07:00","id":109849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=109840#post109840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, I think that you have the Memory status wrong. I read it that you remember past Descents at either Memory 7 or 8.</div> </div> </div> </div>You remember <i>every Descent</i> at Memory 7.<br /> <br /> One dot of Memory below that?<br /> <br /> <i>Two.</i><br /> <br /> At Memory 3 you remember your name, guild, and decree, a little aggregated knowledge of Irem, and the rough details of your previous Descent.<br /> <br /> Everything between 3 and 6 is adding greater degrees of detail on that one preceding Descent along with sketchy bits of others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T09:46:23-07:00","id":110126,"title":"","content":"Really? Because all I see in Memory 3 is that you remember who you are (name and Guild) and I don't see any remembering past Descents until 7. If it says that you partially remember a past Descent, I just assume it's just backwash from the Rite of Return, of how Memory is completely muddled until the high levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:17:07-07:00","id":110150,"title":"","content":"Memory 7: Once a mummy\u2019s Memory has increased to this rank, <b>she remembers every Descent well, except for past thoughts inspired by an even higher Memory.</b> She might remember knowing her original life, but not what that knowledge actually consisted of.<br /> <br /> Memory 6: <b>The Arisen accurately recalls two prior Descents:</b> the one prior to the current one, and one Descent that holds special emotional significance. The mummy cannot remember any information that requires a higher Memory rank to recall. <b>She also remembers fragments of other Descents.</b> Although other parts of her Iremite life are as sketchy as ever, she can now remember every craft or object she made with her own hands.<br /> <br /> Memory 5: <b>The Arisen remembers the previous Descent in great detail and possesses rough knowledge of other arisings, as well.</b> She has learned little of Irem in the journey of Memory, but this is the lowest rank in which she remembers going westward clearly\u2014her soul\u2019s journey, trial, and pronouncement of decree before the unmasked Judges.<br /> <br /> Memory 4: <b>At this rank, a mummy remembers the previous Descent in detail.</b> She also remembers parts of her life in Irem related to friends, family, and work, and glimpses of the day of her Rite. She recalls suffering in Duat and standing before the Judges, but in a more surreal fashion, one that freely injects people and places from past arisings.<br /> <br /> Memory 3: The Arisen remembers her name, guild, and decree. She knows a little about Irem, but cannot easily distinguish between personal experience and what she learned throughout various arisings. <b>She remembers the Descent previous to the current arising in rough detail, though there are gaps in areas where she operated at Memory 6 or higher.</b><br /> <br /> Memory 2: The Arisen remembers her name, guild and decree, and that she was born in or brought into the Nameless Empire in her mortal life, but <b>she does not remember</b> actually living in Irem or <b>anything about subsequent periods of activity except for unintelligible fragments (e.g., sentences from conversations, familiar vessels).</b> She may even invent a delusional history for herself.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T05:45:56-07:00","id":110733,"title":"","content":"Is it really necessary to post the entire reference and not just the page number?? I think most of us have the pdf/pod/prestige.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T09:22:53-07:00","id":110842,"title":"","content":"Guildhalls has a really easy way to deal with the whole guild and nome structure issue, but I still spelled it out in DC. Beyond that, cults are an extension of the Arisen beyond Memory: they, like so many government agencies, have an institutional memory that goes beyond any individual no matter their puissance. As for other supernaturals, no. Space is at a premium, and unless it's a thing like Tome of the Watchtowers doing a blow-by-blow it's not worth the space. Additionally, if Rose or Dave wanted to cover the vampire or Mage side of DC, they'd have to read what we 'd written and it'd constrain them. Beyond that, excepting vampires and relic-fixated hunters the Arisen usually just don't CARE. There's not a huge overlap, and what's there doesn't justify the space. That said, There are hooks if you want to latch Mummy into the greater WoD, but it fits cleanly if you don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:02:39-07:00","id":110883,"title":"","content":"I am really eager to see Necropolis D.C. Any idea when we can finally get the PDF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T10:57:13-07:00","id":110912,"title":"","content":"I think that the general public is fairly comfortable in how single-city necropoli nomes work (though, we don't quite grasp how MANY mummies are in one) because it's largely like a normal tier 2/3 filled city. I'd love more information about rural and large nomes. Would it be wrong to say there are nomes that resemble the Kingdoms of Concordia in oChangeling? Or are they all compact and centered on a city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-11T11:00:39-07:00","id":110918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=110883#post110883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really eager to see Necropolis D.C. Any idea when we can finally get the PDF?</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I understand they are hoping to get it released to at least the kickstarter backers for &quot;proof reading&quot; before the end of April. That's going off of a reply Rich made to a comment on this weeks Monday Meeting Schedule.<br /> <br /> Its got final dev pass, the overall CCP approval and the RPGDrivethru's pdf approval process to go through. I don't know about the dev pass stuff, but I've been CCP approvals take as little as a couple of days and as much as three and a half weeks. Drivethru's one is usually no more then 48 hours in my experience. So its entirely possible that it will be out this month. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T16:50:52-07:00","id":258555,"title":"","content":"What's up, Development Tease thread?!<br /> <br /> The Rio Citybook and Sothis Ascends are being written (as is Dreams of Avarice, if I'm not mistaken?), but Book of the Deceived is in its stretch home. It's been written and is in editing, and its artists have been called to duty.<br /> <br /> Any chance for a quick glimpse of Sixth Guild insights before it's released, hopefully, in a couple months?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T07:40:56-07:00","id":258976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=258555#post258555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's up, Development Tease thread?!<br /> <br /> The Rio Citybook and Sothis Ascends are being written (as is Dreams of Avarice, if I'm not mistaken?), but Book of the Deceived is in its stretch home. It's been written and is in editing, and its artists have been called to duty.<br /> <br /> Any chance for a quick glimpse of Sixth Guild insights before it's released, hopefully, in a couple months?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded! I've been dying for teasers about the Sixth Guild.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2497-brian888","name":"Brian888","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T21:12:51-07:00","id":259477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=258555#post258555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's up, Development Tease thread?!<br /> <br /> The Rio Citybook and Sothis Ascends are being written (as is Dreams of Avarice, if I'm not mistaken?), but Book of the Deceived is in its stretch home. It's been written and is in editing, and its artists have been called to duty.<br /> <br /> Any chance for a quick glimpse of Sixth Guild insights before it's released, hopefully, in a couple months?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ever the optimist Reseru.<br /> <br /> I would not call Book of the Deceived as in its &quot;home stretch&quot; until its in layout with all the art in.<br /> <br /> Considering that Deceived has been &quot;in Editing&quot; for 12 weeks, it seems to have fallen prey the development slippage that the whole line seems to suffer from endemically.<br /> <br /> To give you an idea the estimated &quot;Editing Time&quot; for M20, the largest book that White Wolf/Onyx Path has ever produced is estimated at around 8 weeks from now (having been in editing for about 2/3 before that announcement was made). Rich even mentioned that on average a splat book should be about 4 weeks in editing, with new core books being around 6ish. <br /> <br /> So Deceived seems to have already taken 3 times as long in editing as is normal for a book of its kind. Really the development cycle for this book has been nothing but &quot;cursed&quot; you might say. 8 months in redlines and now 3+ in editing with art only going out to artists this week for pieces beyond the chapter starting art full-page spreads.<br /> <br /> Thank the Judges I'm basically beyond caring about the development issues that wrack the Mummy line. Though apparently not enough to occasionally post semi-whining forum comments it seems :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T22:01:22-07:00","id":259516,"title":"","content":"Being a big fan of Mummy and it's cleverness, yeah, the cursed production of Mummy is a hella taxed. I just want some kind of drop of water in this entire desert of Mummy secrets.<br /> <br /> Acknowledging that I am not as super-attached as some folks though, I say with a mixture of sincerity, compassion, and semi-relief on my part, it must <i>suck</i> to be a superfan of Mummy. The only lines who suffer harder are Geist and Promethean, and the Created have the 2nd Edition to geek out over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T22:51:22-07:00","id":259553,"title":"","content":"Speaking as such a superfan, yeah, it does rather suck. Last I heard, the Book of the Deceived was meant to come out next month, wasn't it? And Sothis Ascends was supposedly December, from memory. I can't say the total silence on either gives me a whole lot of confidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T01:00:06-07:00","id":259606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=259516#post259516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a big fan of Mummy and it's cleverness, yeah, the cursed production of Mummy is a hella taxed. I just want some kind of drop of water in this entire desert of Mummy secrets.<br /> <br /> Acknowledging that I am not as super-attached as some folks though, I say with a mixture of sincerity, compassion, and semi-relief on my part, it must <i>suck</i> to be a superfan of Mummy. The only lines who suffer harder are Geist and Promethean, and the Created have the 2nd Edition to geek out over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its just a person thing for me, but I consider Mummy the most neglected line after Geist.<br /> <br /> I consider Promethean as &quot;more loved&quot; simply because its got its entire book run out and has all the subject matter the game engages with covered by its book line. In addition, its getting a Second Edition which, if its anything like Strix will consolidate all the best bits from the various books and add new, interesting and streamlined stuff. I actually really like that post Second Edition, its entirely likely that Promethean will suffer not one bit for being run out of a single book. <br /> <br /> Mummy on the other hand, well, I've made my view about the way the lines development has been handled known at length on several threads. To sum up, Mummy's been out 18 months and the line is no where near finished its original book run and the games content is still incomplete. <br /> <br /> Compare this to Demon (which is a valid comparison I feel, as they were both &quot;new line&quot; Kickstarted books in the new world of darkness). In the 8 months since its preview release to the Kickstarter backers (and 6 months to the general public) Demon has managed to get all its Kickstarter books out. The Demon lines final book going into production as we speak for likely a January-March release next year. Meaning the entire line is going to be put to likely to be put to bed inside 12 months. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Mummy is only about half way through its Kickstarter reward books (not even that really) and every thing book in the line seems to undergo at least a 6 month delay. At this point I seriously would not be surprised if we see the Beast core book preview pdf for Kickstarter backers get out before the Mummy line has finished. At its current rate Sothis will be released around July next year. Rio around April maybe. Dreams might as well be this time next year. <br /> <br /> I need to stop now, thinking about this stuff again is actually making me angry...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T04:35:15-07:00","id":259687,"title":"","content":"Oh, Hawthorn. Ever the pessimist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Someone here has to keep the love alive (shout-out to homies with the AP threads here).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=259516#post259516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...it must <i>suck</i> to be a superfan of Mummy. The only lines who suffer harder are Geist and Promethean, and the Created have the 2nd Edition to geek out over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, it does suck. Promethean was my favorite line for WoD and is what introduced me to it and the only thing I've run, which I certainly did not have enough time to do. Now WoD is the only RPG I really pay attention to, with occasional other interests that I know I probably won't run. But man, when Mummy was announced and released Promethean became #2 and I wanted to really run something (as in any RPG!) for the first time in like five years.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I've been waiting patiently for Dark Eras, and not any Mummy-specific release, before kicking off the immense campaign I envision <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which...where is the Kickstarter for that? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T09:32:59-07:00","id":259809,"title":"","content":"On the plus side, it seems like whatever speedbumps BotD had have been passed. If the Monday updates are anything to go by its started chugging along again. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T23:26:40-07:00","id":261122,"title":"","content":"I really hope that is the case. I have two players in my game eager to learn secrets of the Deceived, and I'd love to have some idea of what they can do so I can starting feeding them little bits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T04:55:32-07:00","id":261212,"title":"","content":"Well the DC citybook hinted at some stuff for them, regarding the unique nature of their 'relics'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T07:07:07-07:00","id":261239,"title":"","content":"DC had quite a lot of hints about them, yeah. Relic architecture is the big one for my Tef-Aabhi player (for what is likely an obvious reason), and I've been making do with what we know so far. I don't think I'm prepared to do anything with &quot;abstract relics&quot; until we get more information on them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T15:44:55-07:00","id":261563,"title":"","content":"We can't really expect spoilers for Mummy, as theyd have to be a) player and st friendly, and thus nothing with any meat.. Or b) be a real, huge spoilers that only STs should see (and really, what players on the forums wouldnt be tempted). DC gave us enough to go by, but I assume Im not the only ST that has been beating around the bush regarding the Deceived until the book is out. There were recently some big twists in my Mummy game--a traitor high priest Rezzed a mummy on the mission to kill his mortal lover because the lover &quot;heretically seeks the Deceived, to turn you from the Judges&quot;. After evading his attacks, the lover convinced his mummy love to spare his life. This ended with the surprising turn of the Mummy to the hands of the deceived. This, mind you, after the players latched onto the Deceived as the interesting subplot (shuanksen have only been addressed once, and never encountered). I suppose i can try to force some filler, but there are storylines waiting patiently for the Book of the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T17:26:11-07:00","id":261607,"title":"","content":"Well it can't hurt to begin introducing them into the campaign(s), right? It's not like you'll want to spill all their deep dark secrets to your PCs right away anyway, and the book will be (hopefully) out soon enough. They are, more or less, Deathless rather than Lifeless, so just using the default Arisen mechanics should suffice for now. Otherwise, just have them, you know, be mysterious and sinister <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It's not like a year ago when you simply couldn't use the Deceived because of lack of information","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T02:50:40-07:00","id":261972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/106733-development-tease-cursed-necropolis-d-c?p=261607#post261607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like a year ago when you simply couldn't use the Deceived because of lack of information</div> </div> </div> </div>I am so tempted to ask if that should be taken with a healthy dose of sarcasm...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> True DC did make it so we had ANYTHING about the Deceived except the most scant rumours that could be dropped into the background of a game. Which is all we had for over a year of the games publication. Now you can tease them with some more solid ideas about their abilities and the sort of stuff they seem to do, but its still not exactly the sort of stuff that means you can drop a fully stated Deceived NPC into a game. <br /> <br /> As for the release, I'm betting mid-November at best, 4-6 weeks for the art to come in, editing to (finally) be over and layout to happen. This is literally my best case scenario however. <br /> <br /> Damn, sound bitter again...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T04:58:50-07:00","id":262017,"title":"","content":"Hum...I don't know? Haha. I mean, I think I meant it seriously but with a tinge of resentfulness? I know information on the Deceived isn't, you know, at all significant, but it's better than the absolutely nothing on them in the core book. It's also better than a year ago in that we're only a few months from the supplement's release rather than over a year, which is how I mostly meant it. You know, so like it's better now because if you start seeding your campaign with more hints then by the time your PCs start deserving some answers then the book will hopefully be out by then.<br /> <br /> A year ago you couldn't risk that, but now you can I guess?<br /> <br /> I certainly plan on using the Sixth Guild in my planned campaign, but it's so chock full of demons, Shuankhsen, Underworld journeys, vampires, werewolves, and Frankenstein's monster as it is that I'm not even worried about Deceived right now. There's plenty of other things to use for inspiration in the meantime. But yes, it is unfortunate that people who wanted Deceived weren't able to use them right away :\\","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T06:26:39-07:00","id":262088,"title":"","content":"For my part, the Deceived aren't as important in and of themselves as antagonists. If they were just another kind of Shuankhsen, angry, possibly insane, behind-the-scenes villains with links to Irem's past, they would be a cool option but not terribly evocative by themselves. We already have something in that vein.<br /> <br /> The Deceived are more interesting for the promise of experimentation, for something a little more free-form in terms of magic. As a Storyteller, I'm more interested in them for the potential for forbidden knowledge my players could learn. Things like the Relic Architecture in Cursed Necropolis D.C. and the myriad references to True Name Magic. I'm really hoping for a juicy set of mechanics that could give things like grand Tef-Aabhi projects more mechanical heft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}